        ["I188"] = "←The Palace of Wind\nRalugo→",
        ["I189"] = "DANGER!",
        ["I190"] = "Gullick's Shop",
        ["I191"] = "Jens, the Blacksmith",
        ["I195"] = "Captain's Room",
        ["I196"] = "Commander's Room",
        ["I205"] = "To Alexander,\nI am taking my son and\ngoing to Granatyki.\nGigi",
        ["I206"] = "I found the crown of\nIchrius, but it was taken\naway from me....I can't\nfind my father. Boy, it's\nbeen rough!",
        ["I225"] = "I have come to know your\ntruth. Though I am to\nimpart the great power,\nthis power is not made\navailable. It must be\nproclaimed that the one who\nwaits in the Land of the\nBeginning shall...",
        ["I226"] = "My son, as the new King,\nyou must watch over the\nHoly Sword and protect the\npeople of your kingdom.",
        ["I227"] = "I have lost my bow.\nI haven't been able to\nlocate Promeus.",
        ["I230"] = "Throne of Ichrius",
        ["I235"] = "Lake Noel",
        ["I236"] = "Danger\nDo Not Look",
        ["I237"] = "The Land of Garan",
        ["I238"] = "Varde's House→",
        ["I239"] = "←Varde's House",
        ["I240"] = "Olivier Veyrac, the Swordsmaster\nRest in Peace",
        ["I241"] = "The Nation's Future Lies\nin Your Hands\nAlexander Thornton Regginis",
        ["I242"] = "The Queen of Verdite\nNoel Forester",
        ["I243"] = "Buried in the Darkness\nPrince Austin Lyle Forester",
        ["I244"] = "Rest in Peace\nRojee",
        ["I245"] = "Vice Commander Caine\nForever We Shall Lift Up Your Flame",
        ["I246"] = "Road Sign",
        ["I247"] = "The Cave of Shudom",
        ["I248"] = "The Emblem of the Wind",
        ["I249"] = "Skeleton",
        ["I250"] = "The Statue of the Hero",
        ["I251"] = "Holy King Jean Alfred Forester I",
        ["I252"] = "The Royal Emblem",
        ["I253"] = "Marilyn's Son",
        ["I254"] = "Picture of a Warrior",
        ["I255"] = "Broken Cart",
        ["I256"] = "Animal's Skeleton",
        ["I257"] = "The Dead Body of Nora",
        ["I258"] = "A Wrecked Ship",
        ["I259"] = "The Tomb of the Samurai",
        ["I260"] = "The Dead Body of Leon",
        ["I261"] = "The Tomb of Leon",
        ["I262"] = "The Tomb of Rojee",
        ["I263"] = "The Skeleton of the Giant",
        ["I264"] = "The Dead Body of Sal",
        ["I265"] = "The Dead Body of Endt",
        ["I266"] = "The Dead Body of Lyn",
        ["I267"] = "Yvette Bince",
        ["I268"] = "The Skeleton of Elrus",
        ["I269"] = "The Statue of Warren",
        ["I270"] = "Christy Clements\nShe once had a business near the\ncastle. On the day of the Seal,\nshe followed Leon here, but her\nfamily fled to Granatyki. She\nhas been longing to be reunited\nwith her family and return to her\nlife of optimism and prosperity.",
        ["I271"] = "Lyn Reinhardt\nShe is an elf who used to visit\nthe castle with her father. He\nwent to Garan to look for Promeus\nand never returned. She plans to\ngo in search of him. You and she\nwere friends as children.",
        ["I272"] = "Lyn Reinhardt\nShe is an elf who used to visit\nthe castle with her father. He\nwent to Garan to look for Promeus\nand never returned. She plans to\ngo in search of him. You and she\nwere friends as children.",
        ["I273"] = "Gullick Risty\nA Dwarf who once searched for\nPromeus, he's a merchant now, and\nis one of the last 2 survivors in\nGaran. He sells and buys various\ncollectibles -- as well as a very\nelusive key. He wishes that he\ncould sell Jens' bow.",
        ["I274"] = "Jens Stensland\nHe is a great blacksmith. His\nancestors were the best in the\nworld. Jens hates visitors and\nwon't help anyone unless he's\ngiven Promeus. With it, he makes\nexquisite armor. He quit making\nweapons after his son's death.",
        ["I275"] = "Rene Thomas\nOwner for 50 years, he remains at\nthe inn even though business is\ndead. The King stayed here once,\nbut Rene never mentions it now. A\nbit neurotic these days, he now\nsucks on a dry pipe. There's no-\nthing in it, he's just strange.",
        ["I276"] = "Mlichael Hansen\nAs the birthplace of the King,\nMlichael's hotel used to be packed\nwith visitors. He's a good source\nof information for this reason.\nHis father had a statue of King\nAlfred carved in front of the inn\nbut someone has cut off its face.",
        ["I277"] = "Janan Green\nIn her youth, she tried to get\ninto the men's garrison. She was\ncaught and publicly humiliated by\nthe Kjng. Now her husband has\ndied in battle. Needless to say,\nshe despises the Kjng and wishes\nhim (and the royal family) dead.",
        ["I278"] = "Mark Johnson\nPriests of the past have suffered\nmuch from kings, and so no longer\nkeep written records. Mark had to\nmemorize every known item in the\nuniverse. He rebinds jokebooks in\nleather covers in his spare time,\nbut he is very wise & respected.",
        ["I279"] = "Calmathar\nThe Archmage of Wind, he is the\nonly one who can go in and out of\nthe Palace of Wind built by Kjng\nHarvine. He and John Creel have\nbeen known to play a mean game of\ntwister when times get slow (it's\nbeen around for eons in valicia).",
        ["I280"] = "Garnabus\nThe Archmage of Fire.\nFavorite animal: Fire-Drake\nFavorite food: Cayenne Peppers\nFavorite color: Red\nFavorite pastimes: Roasting\nmarshmallows -- anywhere,\nanytime!",
        ["I281"] = "Ungrund\nThe laziest of the Archmages,\nUngrund created the Golems to find\nPromeus for him. He left Verdite\nfor Mlelanat Island when the\nGolems took over his laboratory\nand tried to kill him. He left\na powerful weapon and a ring...",
        ["I282"] = "Zul Arifin\nThe Archmage of Water, Zul is\nalso known as the Archmage of\nhealing. She holds the key to the\nbridges necessary to cross Lake\nNoel, but without the right\nboots, the bridges are useless to\nyou anyway.",
        ["I283"] = "Varde\nChief of Woods, Varde remains in\nthe forest. He was a friend of\nIchrius, and he likes to play\ntricks on humans -- particularly\nspineless cowards like the King's\nmessenger Robert Shreve. He holds\na very important item and map.",
        ["I284"] = "Jack Leininger\nA resident of Verdite for over 90\nyears, Jack is determined to stay\neven though evil abounds here.\nJack has gotten rather old and\ntends to fall asleep in the middle\nof conversations. He is a good\nsource of information though.",
        ["I285"] = "Airon Green\nHis father was killed in battle a\nfew years ago, but his mother\nhasn't told him. He treasures the\ndagger his father made for him.\nHe's adventurous and mischievous\nHe collects rare items when he's\nnot hunting for trouble.",
        ["I286"] = "Marcus Peppers\nWhile living in the north, he\nturned down an offer to join the\ngarrison to journey to Garan in\nsearch of Promeus. He is a loner\nand will do anything to get what\nhe wants. He tried to sell his\nbaby sister to buy his 1st sword.",
        ["I287"] = "Jamie Porter\nAs a soldier in the garrison, he\nfled during the final battle. An\narbalest bolt grazed his arm and\nthat's his excuse for fleeing in\nterror. Guilt for his cowardice\nled him to gluttony. He's looking\nfor a chance to redeem himself.",
        ["I288"] = "Yvette Bince\nAlex trapped her fiance, Sal, in\nthe castle with the king and, of\ncourse, she's very angry at him\nfor this. She has a key that you\nwill need, but you'll have to\nlisten to her sob story first...\nfeign interest.",
        ["I289"] = "Toni Gomez\nSurviving her parents with her\nsister, Priscilla, Toni is trying\nto protect her sister by rescuing\nCommander Veyrac. She prays for\npeace to return soon, & she does\nnot know how her family made its\nfortune. She holds a rare item...",
        ["I290"] = "Priscilla Gomez\nHer parents were caught shipping\nthe blood sucking plant out of\nRalugo and were executed. The two\ngirls don't know what happened to\ntheir parents. Priscilla awaits\ntheir return. (Toni told her that\nthey'd be back soon.)",
        ["I291"] = "Marilyn Mliller\nShe closed her northern beach inn\nto go in search of her son. She\nlost contact with him and regrets\nnot giving him the charm she made\nfor him before he left. It would\nprotect his soul if he was ever\ncaught. She holds a great reward.",
        ["I292"] = "Ed Edmund\nOnce a grave digger in a nearby\nvillage, he promised Silviera\nthat he would care for the fallen\nsoldiers. He's not getting paid\nto do this, so don't be surprised\nif he offers to sell you an item\nhe lifted from a dead soldier.",
        ["I293"] = "Robert Shreve\nHe writes bad poetry and songs\nabout historical events. The King\nentrusted him with the Eye of\nIchrius but a fairy stole it from\nhim. He's generally spineless,\nbut he did wait 17 years to beg\nfor your mercy.",
        ["I294"] = "Krone Licht\nHe's a historian who's been doing\nresearch on Orladin. Even after\nthe country became a wasteland &\nthe demons became rampant, he has\nstill remained earnestly devoted\nto research and study. He has a\nlot of good information for you.",
        ["I295"] = "Jane Cowley\nShe was a talented stone mason in\nthe north, but her anger brought\nher here where she dresses as a\nboy in hopes of infiltrating the\ngarrison. (I guess she hasn't met\nJanan Green.) If she succeeds,\nshe plans to kill the Kjng.",
        ["I296"] = "John Creel\nGuardian of the Palace of Wind\nfor over 300 years, his one wish\nhas always been to have a puppy.\nBut alas, King Harvine wouldn't\nallow it, poor John. If someone\ncan re-illuminate the palace,\nmaybe his wish will come true.",
        ["I297"] = "Olivier Veyrac\nA childhood friend of the King,\nhe is the Sword Master who was\nentrusted with Ichrius' Wing. He\ntook Lyle out of the castle the\nnight before the seal and asked\nLeon to look after him. He was\nturned to stone shortly after.",
        ["I298"] = "Sal Estrada\nTrapped in the castle at the time\nof the seal, Sal longs to see his\nfiancee again. He and his friend,\nEndt, have been dining on rats\nand scraps of moldy bread for ten\nyears -- he dreams of a big juicy\nsteak! (Oh ya', and Yvette.)",
        ["I299"] = "The Skeleton of the Giant\nRemaining chained to his Earthly\nremains, he is the only Giant\nwhose soul remains in the cave of\nShudom. He mourns his brothers\nwho were all killed by the\ngolems. He is a key to power --\nif you'll do his bidding...",
        ["I300"] = "The Skeleton of Light\nControlled by the will of Guyra,\nhe remains undead until his task\nhas been completed. He was the\nLight Family's third generation\nheir before his death. He still\nretains the power to bestow light\non objects until his soul rests.",
        ["I301"] = "The Tree of Dragon King Plant\nThe materialization of the will\nof Vallad, the tree will impart\nthe knowledge and power of the\ngods upon the Chosen One. Ichrius\nand Orladin received their powers\nhere, and it now awaits Lyle.\nThis is imperative to your quest!",
        ["I302"] = "Leon Shore\nAn infinite source of knowledge,\nLeon is the expert craftsman who\nbefriended Alexander on Mlelanat.\nHe has been protecting the Prince\nfor 10 years. If necessary, he is\nwilling to give his own life for\nthe success of Lyle's quest.",
        ["I303"] = "Leon Shore\nAn infinite source of knowledge,\nLeon is the expert craftsman who\nbefriended Alexander on Mlelanat.\nHe has been protecting the Prince\nfor 10 years. If necessary, he is\nwilling to give his own life for\nthe success of Lyle's quest.",
        ["I304"] = "Leon Shore\nAn infinite source of knowledge,\nLeon is the expert craftsman who\nbefriended Alexander on Mlelanat.\nHe has been protecting the Prince\nfor 10 years. If necessary, he is\nwilling to give his own life for\nthe success of Lyle's quest.",
        ["I305"] = "Orladin\nThe master Archmage, he commanded\nall 5 elements of power. Also a\nwicked prankster, he once sent a\nbaby dragon disguised as a puppy\nto the King of Wind. When half of\nthe palace was destroyed, Harvine\nvowed to never have another dog.",
        ["I306"] = "Airon Green\nHis father was killed in battle a\nfew years ago, but his mother\nhasn't told him. He treasures the\ndagger his father made for him.\nHe's adventurous and mischievous\nHe collects rare items when he's\nnot hunting for trouble.",
        ["I307"] = "Janan Green\nIn her youth, she tried to get\ninto the men's garrison. She was\ncaught and publicly humiliated by\nthe Kjng. Now her husband has\ndied in battle. Needless to say,\nshe despises the Kjng and wishes\nhim (and the royal family) dead.",
        ["I308"] = "Joe Santos\nHe escaped from the mental hos-\npital in Granatyki. His \"vision\"\nfrom vallad told him to come here\nin search of the key to the trea-\nsure of the Light Family. He's\ngotten better, he used to think\nhe was a glass of orange juice.",
        ["I309"] = "Franz Stoppenbach\nA follower of Krone Licht, he was\nleft behind when demons showed up\nin the Path of Thieves. He fought\nthem off long enough for Licht to\nget away, but hasn't been able to\nmove to catch up with him since.\nHe worries about his teacher.",
        ["I310"] = "Tim Lindquist\nAfter he tried to start a home\nsecurity business using rattle-\nsnakes, he was chased out of his\nhome village. He's now a travel-\ning merchant who roams from\ntown to town awaiting his next\ngreat inspiration.",
        ["I311"] = "James Seward MoCain V\nOnce a proud soldier, he is now\nbitter and angry over his plight.\nHe was wounded in battle and is\nangry that he didn't die from his\ninjury. He wishes for death, but\nfor the sake of honor, he can't\ntake his own life.",
        ["I312"] = "Alexander Thornton Regginis\nHe is the Prince of Granatyki,\nchampion of King Alfred, savior\nof the Moleonlight Sword, and hero\nof Verdite. But he's also dead.\nSorry, the fate of the kingdom is\nstill in your hands...even\nAlexander is counting on you.",
        ["I313"] = "Mlel Molerris\nObsessed with Gigi on the island\nof Mlelanat, he followed her here\nwhen she moved to Verdite. He was\ngoing to ask her out, but she was\nafraid of him and ran away during\nthe commotion following the Great\nSeal. He longs to see her again.",
        ["I320"] = "Mantrap\nA gigantic, carnivorous plant\nwith many different sub-species.\nMantrap is mobile and preys on\nany living organism that produces\nheat. Head Eater, which can\nswallow a whole human being, is\none variation of this plant.",
        ["I321"] = "Mantrap\nA gigantic, carnivorous plant\nwith many different sub-species.\nMantrap is mobile and preys on\nany living organism that produces\nheat. Head Eater, which can\nswallow a whole human being, is\none variation of this plant.",
        ["I322"] = "Head Eater\nA sub-species of Mantrap, Head\nEater restricts its diet to man.\nWhen a Head Eater swallows a\nperson, they are swallowed whole,\nand the person inside is kept\nthere indefinitely without being\ndigested. Some made it their\nprofession to hunt Head Eaters.",
        ["I323"] = "Grave Pot\nIt does not possess any means of\ndirect attack. Instead, it gives\nout poison to anyone who comes\ninto contact with it. In case of\ndirect contact, the poison will\nprevail. Its weakness is fire.",
        ["I324"] = "Two Headed Grave Pot\nA different variety of Grave Pot,\nthis one has two heads instead of\none to spew out poison\nalternately. Its weakness is also\nfire.",
        ["I325"] = "Reaper\nA living organism made up of\nseveral hands. It is neither\nplant nor animal. Because of its\naffinity for people, gold coins\nand jewelry are often discovered\nin its stomach.",
        ["I326"] = "Log Stalker\nThe dried up logs in the woods\nbecame living things after the\nKing's dramatic change. They were\npossessed by demons and now will\nassault people with magic and\nwith their sharp branches. Their\nweakness is fire.",
        ["I327"] = "Stool\nA poisonous mushroom, Stool's\nperimeter of attack is limited.\nDon't be fooled by its innocent\nappearance, it's VERY poisonous!\nThe best defense against its\npoison is to have a weapon with a\nlong reach, or to use magic.",
        ["I328"] = "Para Stool\nA different variety of Stool, the\nPara Stool emits poison which\ncauses complete paralysis. One\nmust stay away from it by any\nmeans. Effective attacks are the\nsame as for Stool.",
        ["I329"] = "Mummy\nIn the past in Verdite,\nmummification was practiced for\nburial. Since the King's undoing,\nthe Mummies have been called back\nfrom the grave. Once it is\nawakened, it will attack whoever\ndisturbed its sleep.",
        ["I330"] = "Skeletons\nThe bones of the ancient soldiers\nin Verdite are now controlled by\nthe minions of evil. They have no\nthought or will of their own.\nSome are actually made out of\nclay that probably contained\nancient bones of soldiers.",
        ["I331"] = "Skull Soldiers\nThose knights who fought as\nsoldiers for Verdite and died in\nbattle have been resurrected by\nthe King to do his evil bidding.",
        ["I332"] = "Skull Masters\nThey are powerful skeletons which\nused to be warlocks. During their\nlifetime of strict discipline,\nsome were tempted to the evil\npath of magic. After death these\nunfortunate souls wander as the\nundead. Their weakness is fire.",
        ["I333"] = "Undead Born\nUnlike other skeletons, these are\nsimply ghosts. They lack\noffensive power. They were\nprobably ordinary citizens before\ntheir death.",
        ["I334"] = "Clay Golem\nEvil creatures created out of\nclay by Shudom, they multiplied\ntoo rapidly and began to lose\ntheir intelligence. Shudom\nabandoned them when the Golems\nbegan to attack him.",
        ["I335"] = "Promeus Golem\nThe Golems were created to find\nPromeus for Shudom. Once the\nGolem finds it, the Promeus is\nintegrated into the Golem's body.\nA Promeus Golem is immune to most\nattacks and magics of the earth.\nIt has a most effective defense.",
        ["I336"] = "Grave Shadow\nThey began to appear after the\nKing's transformation. They have\nno thought of their own, only\nscattered and fragmented thoughts\nwith the instinct to kill by the\nonly means they have.",
        ["I337"] = "Race\nThese are a stronger, more\nintelligent version of the Grave\nShadow. Race wander around\nseeking to be embodied in the\nliving.",
        ["I338"] = "Hell Worms\nThey dwell in the land of Garan\nand have large, strong jaws with\nbig, poisoned teeth. Hell Worms\nconsume the earth as their source\nof nourishment, and oftentimes,\nVerdite and other forms of jewels\ncan be found in their bodies.",
        ["I339"] = "Red Eye\nBefore the Day of the Seal, it\nwas a normal spider. Since then,\nit has increased in size to a\nhuge monster that will come out\nof its nest to attack people and\nother animals. Its weakness is\nthe magical power of water.",
        ["I340"] = "Poison Red Eye\nThis is the other variation of\nthe Red Eye. It has an equally\nnasty bite, but this one also\ncontains poison. Like the Red\nEye, its weakness is the magical\npower of water.",
        ["I341"] = "Shell Dragon\nResembling a big turtle, Shell\nDragon is impermeable once in a\ndefensive position. Because of\nhis defensive shell, it is also\nimpossible to attack from the\nside or back. Not to worry, a\nfront attack won't hurt -- much.",
        ["I342"] = "Garan Lizard\nGiant lizards in leather armor,\nthey live in the valley of Garan\nattacking those who come seeking\nthe precious metal, Promeus. Upon\nkilling them, you can see they\nalso have a voracious appetite\nfor human flesh.",
        ["I343"] = "Death Knight\nUnlike the Death Fighter, the\nDeath Knight used to be a Knight\nof noble origin. He's a tremen-\ndous fighter with high magical\npower and is one of the most\nperfectly balanced undead\ncreatures serving Seath.",
        ["I344"] = "Imperial Guards\nThey are the knights selected to\nprotect the King. They will never\nretreat in battle and are highly\nmotivated with undivided loyalty\nto the King. Tragically they\nended up following the Evil King\nwithout hesitation.",
        ["I345"] = "Imperial Guards\nThey are the knights selected to\nprotect the King. They will never\nretreat in battle and are highly\nmotivated with undivided loyalty\nto the King. Tragically they\nended up following the Evil King\nwithout hesitation.",
        ["I346"] = "Gatekeepers\nThese are dead bodies of those\nwho died protecting the castle.\nThese ghosts have only one\nthought, that is, they will do\nanything to protect the castle.",
        ["I347"] = "Guards\nThese semi-living creatures were\ncreated by Orladin to be his\nservants. Even after the death of\nOrladin, they have been doing\ntheir odd jobs. They possess no\noffensive power but have strong\nlife power.",
        ["I348"] = "Guards\nThese semi-living creatures were\ncreated by Orladin to be his\nservants. Even after the death of\nOrladin, they have been doing\ntheir odd jobs. They possess no\noffensive power but have strong\nlife power.",
        ["I349"] = "Wall Ghost\nThose living in the castle were\nbound inside the walls by an evil\nspell.",
        ["I350"] = "Crooked Demon\nKing Harvine created these evil\ncreatures which possess the power\nof wind. Some lost control due to\nthe existing power of the island,\nand after sacrificing many\nsoldiers, Harvine was forced to\ndestroy them.",
        ["I351"] = "Ichrius' Guards\nThey were created along with\nIchrius' equipment and their duty\nis to protect this equipment.\nThey have highly skilled\nfighting abilities and cannot\nbe defeated easily.",
        ["I352"] = "Crannell\nCreated by Orladin, it possesses\nhigh intelligence and powerful\nmagic. Its life force is weak,\nbut magic is ineffective against\nit, so you must approach it with\na sword. Getting close to it will\nbe difficult.",
        ["I353"] = "Polaris\nAlso known as the Ice Demon, it\nhas the powers of wind and water.\nUnder the King's power, it killed\nmany people before the Day of the\nSeal. Since then, it has been\nfrozen and will remain thus until\nits master's command awakens it.",
        ["I354"] = "Raymire\nIt is an evil creature created by\nOrladin to defend the stationary\nposts. It has water power and\nresistance against ordinary\nweapons.",
        ["I355"] = "Alchemine\nIt is an evil creature created by\nOrladin. It has fire power and\nresistance against magic. It\nprotects the maze palace of\nOrladin by sneaking behind\ntrespassers and killing them\nwithout a sound.",
        ["I356"] = "Demon Lord\nHe is an evil creature created\nmainly by Guyra. There are\nseveral variations. This type is\nthe final, perfected variation.",
        ["I357"] = "Garan Tess\nThey were the descendants of the\nlegendary tribe of Garan. Unlike\ntheir ancestors who refused to\nuse magic and fought with their\nown physical strength, Garan Tess\nwill use the magic of earth.",
        ["I358"] = "Skull Fighters\nSpirits of those who died but\nwere prevented from dying.\nThey will commence repeated\nattacks against any casting of\na spell. They sometimes appear\nin the form of a loved one or\neven ones' self.",
        ["I359"] = "Gasts\nThey are the spirits of those who\ndied in fear. They attack not\nbecause of hatred but because the\nfear forces them to.",
        ["I360"] = "Death Fighter\nDeath Fighters are the armor of\nsoldiers killed by Black Knights.\nThey are controlled by Seath, and\nhave risen to fight again --\nremembering the hatred they died\nwith. They are quick and will not\ncease fighting until destroyed.",
        ["I361"] = "Scythe\nA demon summoned by Garnabus,\nScythe has a high intelligence &\ncan use various magic attacks. He\nattacks opponents with a large\nScythe that paralyzes enemies and\nthen continues attacking them\nafter they are stunned.",
        ["I362"] = "Living Statue\nThe stone statue which was given\nlife through a spell. He makes an\nexcellent guard, for he simply\nstands as a stone until an\ninvader appears. He is high on\ndefense and low on offense.",
        ["I363"] = "Lua Stone\nA long time ago, a shrine was\nerected to honor Turcotte\nIchrius, a High Elf. The stone\nstatue created to guard this\ntemple is called Lua Stone.",
        ["I364"] = "Puppet\nPuppet is a doll, but Orladin\ngave life to it. It moves around\nbut is not effective as an\noffensive or defensive fighter.",
        ["I365"] = "Blood Demon\nHe started out as a fairly small\ndemon but has steadily increased\nin size as he has gobbled up the\nsouls of people in the castle.\nHis favorite tactic is to drag\nthe enemies into utter darkness\nand then devour them.",
        ["I366"] = "Blood Demon\nHe started out as a fairly small\ndemon but has steadily increased\nin size as he has gobbled up the\nsouls of people in the castle.\nHis favorite tactic is to drag\nthe enemies into utter darkness\nand then devour them.",
        ["I367"] = "DragoNewt\nHe is not an evil creature but\nwill obey the DragoMaster. He is\na combination of man and dragon.\nHis creator is called the Dragon\nof Fire. This is assumed by\nobserving his power of fire.",
        ["I368"] = "DragoMaster\nThis is a title of very high\nrank. No one knows why Drago\nNewt, who is more powerful than\nthe King, obeys King Alfred who\nis merely a human.",
        ["I369"] = "Merrill Ur\nHe used to be admired by many\nElves because of his devotion to\nSeath and his superior fighting\nskills. He is now dreaded as he\ncame back as an \"Undead\". He\nwanders around mournfully seeking\nGuyra's will in the cemetery.",
        ["I370"] = "Jean Alfred Forester, the\nSwordsmaster\nThe son of Houser Forester, he\nwas crowned Kjng of verdite when\nhe saved the kingdom from the\ndemons which arose from the royal\ncemetery. He is called the Holy\nKjng because he obtained the Holy\nSword of Lght, \"Moonlight Sword.\"",
        ["I371"] = "Seath\nSeath, the White Dragon who was\nworshipped by the High Elves, was\ncreated hen Vallad split himself\ninto two beings. Seath and Guyra\nforgot their missions soon after\nbeing created and began an epic\nbattle for control of the world.",
        ["I372"] = "Garth\nArchmages all make similar\ncreatures for defense and for\ndecorations. Garth was created\nby Shudom. He is an imitation\nof Thedek, but is quite inferior\nto him.",
        ["I373"] = "Graine\nHe was created by Orladin to\nprotect his Maze Temple. All\nthe creatures of this type have\na common weakness. They are\ndefenseless against arrows.",
        ["I374"] = "Face Trap\nOrladin's subordinates set this\ntrap. If anyone comes within\nsight of it, the door will open\nautomatically, and the Face will\ncome out and assault the\nintruder with arrows.",
        ["I375"] = "Salamanders\nThese are made by Thedek, Fire\nMage, as a room decoration.\nThese decorations, after their\nmaster went into hiding, began to\nspew fire at anything that moves.",
        ["I376"] = "Skull Trap\nThese traps have the shape\nof skeletons, but they are not\nreal bones -- they were made\nby Orladin to cast the spell\nof darkness on intruders.",
        ["I377"] = "Virulents\nThese creatures were created by\nGarnabus to be his bodyguards.\nThey are defenseless against\narrows.",
        ["I378"] = "Gables\nThedek made these for King\nHarvine. Unfortunately, they\nwere not very useful -- They are\neasily destroyed by arrows.",
        ["I379"] = "Flare\nThe Maze Temple of Orladin is\nnot connected to the lava flow.\nThis must have come in from a\ndifferent source.",
        ["I380"] = "Eye of Crown\nThis shadow will appear as it\nsynchronizes with the Vision of\nCrown.",
        ["I381"] = "Statue of the Hero\nThe stone statue of Silviera was\nbuilt by those saved by the\ncourageous Commander. Silviera\nwent into the castle and has\nnever returned. The people who\nbuilt the statue are mostly gone\nnow.",
        ["I384"] = "Wind Candlestick\nIt was made by Thedek, Fire\nMage, for King Harvine. After\nthe death of Thedek, this living\ncandlestick has been waiting for\nsomeone to come to light its\ncandle.",
        ["I385"] = "Wind Candlestick\nIt was made by Thedek, Fire\nMage, for King Harvine. After\nthe death of Thedek, this living\ncandlestick has been waiting for\nsomeone to come to light its\ncandle.",
        ["I386"] = "Green Slime\nThey hate direct sunlight and so\nlive in dark, wet areas. The\ncrescent axe and fire are the\nmost effective weapons against\nthem. They have antidote fluid\ninside, so if you're poisoned,\nlet them bite you for a cure.",
        ["I390"] = "Special Weapon   94 cm  0.9kg\nThis is the greatest achievement of\nLeon Shore. This is the first stage\nof the sword which will grow more\npowerful as the owner uses it.",
        ["I391"] = "Special Weapon   128 cm  2.5kg\nThe 2nd stage of Leon's greatest\nsword. It has grown 26 cm.and it\nweighs 1.6 kg more than in the 1st\nstage. It will continue to grow.",
        ["I392"] = "Special Weapon   156 cm  3.3kg\nThe final stage of Excellector, the\nsword now has the power of light.\nIt will be needed to make the\nIchrius' Key.",
        ["I393"] = "Ordinary Weapon  118 cm  1.3kg\nThis ordinary weapon is issued\nto all of the soldiers in the\nVerdite Army.",
        ["I394"] = "Ordinary Weapon  118 cm  1.3kg\nThis weapon possesses the power of\nlight. It is a long sword with a\nscarlet blade which was carried by\nCaine, vice commander to Silviera.",
        ["I395"] = "Ordinary Weapon  136 cm  2.8kg\nThe Long Sword was designed for\nupper class swordsmen, but the\nBroad Sword was used by squad\nleaders because of its reach.",
        ["I396"] = "Ordinary Weapon  136cm  2.4kg\nThis sword was created for the 3\npeople other than Houser Forester\nwho were granted the title of Sword\nMaster. It has the power of light.",
        ["I397"] = "Ordinary Weapon  126cm  1.2kg\nThis is an easy sword for\nbeginners to learn with. It is\nslender and is used for\nthrusting.",
        ["I398"] = "Special Weapon   130cm  1.3kg\nThis sword was given to King\nHarvine by the King of the East.The\nRyu-ga has an extremely sharp blade.\nIt has the magical power of wind.",
        ["I399"] = "Special Weapon  163cm  6.8kg\nThis is a sword of Promeus. It was\ngiven to Silviera but has remained\nunused since his disappearance.",
        ["I400"] = "Special Weapon  128cm  3.1kg\nThis is the sword used by the\npeople of the land of Garan where\nthe Dwarfs reside at present. The\nsword has the earth power.",
        ["I401"] = "Special Weapon  135cm  4.Okg\nIt is the sword of flame and has\nthe power of fire. The Fire of\nAnor is built inside its blade.",
        ["I402"] = "Special Weapon  131cm  3.3kg\nAs a result of receiving the\nwater blessing, this sword\nacquired the power of water. It\nhas a tremendous striking power.",
        ["I403"] = "Special Weapon  130cm  4.8kg\nThe sword of Mlerrill Ur, hero of\nthe High Elves. This sword has the\nsharpest blade of all the weapons.\nIt was presented to Ur by Seath.",
        ["I404"] = "Special Weapon  165cm  1.6kg\nLeon Shore made this sword out of\nthe black crystal left behind by\nGuyra. It contains all the\nmagical power except light.",
        ["I405"] = "Special Weapon  151cm  1.6kg\nThis sword was discovered by King\nAlfred in the cemetery. It has the\npower of light and also has the\nability to heal its user.",
        ["I406"] = "Special Weapon  142cm  1.2kg\nVallad made this sword with the\nlight magic. The famous holy sword,\nowned by King Alfred, will\nrevitalize man's spirit and health.",
        ["I407"] = "Special Weapon  152cm  1.4kg\nVallad made this sword. The spirit\nof King Alfred added more light\npower to the sword as a gift to his\nson who released him.",
        ["I410"] = "Ordinary Weapon   108cm  2.4 kg\nThe axe is light but the blow it\ngives is heavier than a sword.\nThis Axe is a good weapon for\nthose of strength.",
        ["I411"] = "Ordinary Weapon   174cm  3.5 kg\nIt is a battle axe with a\nconsiderably longer reach.\nIt overwhelms enemies with\nits reach and striking power.",
        ["I412"] = "Special Weapon    174cm  7.O kg\nThe axe has great striking\npower, but it is cursed. The axe\nmay sometimes cast a spell upon its\nuser, paralyzing him.",
        ["I413"] = "Special Weapon    183cm  4.O kg\nAn earth spirit embodied itself\nwithin its blade. The weapon has\nthe power of earth and an\nextremely sharp edge.",
        ["I414"] = "Ordinary Weapon   164cm  0.7 kg\nEven those who lack in physical\nstrength can swing this light\nweight club to fight in a battle.",
        ["I417"] = "Ordinary Weapon   120cm  1.O kg\nThis large Bow is used to shoot\ndown the enemies who are scaling\nthe castle wall.",
        ["I418"] = "Special Weapon    150cm  1.5 kg\nThe great blacksmith Jens Stensland\nswore off weapons after making this\nbow. Its arrow follows the target\nforever. It saps its users energy.",
        ["I419"] = "Ordinary Weapon    93cm  1.8 kg\nThe club has an iron star shaped\nball attached to its tip.",
        ["I420"] = "Ordinary Weapon    93cm  1.5 kg\nIt is a Morning Star sword made\nof silver, the special metal for\nthose in sacred professions. It\nhas the power of light.",
        ["I421"] = "Special Weapon     93cm  3.2 kg\nThis weapon will suck the life from\nyour enemy and convert it into the\nuser's life power. It has its good\npoints, but it forfeits magic use.",
        ["I422"] = "Special Weapon    105cm  0.7 kg\nThis weapon has magic of water &\nwill increase the power of magic.\nIt has no power for striking, but\nwill cast a powerful spell instead.",
        ["I423"] = "Special Weapon    105cm  0.7 kg\nIt carries the magic of fire and\nwill increase the power of magic\nfor its user. It has no striking\npower, but will cast a spell.",
        ["I424"] = "Ordinary Armor   Head  1.O kg\nThis helmet is standard issue to\nall the soldiers of the Verdite\nArmy. It is not very effective\nas a defensive gear.",
        ["I425"] = "Ordinary Armor   Head  1.O kg\nA stronger helm than the standard\nleather Helm, the Iron Helm was\nused by the armored infantry of\nthe Verdite Army.",
        ["I426"] = "Ordinary Armor   Head  2.5 kg\nThe helm was used by upper class\nsoldiers to demonstrate their high\nrank. Only selected soldiers were\nallowed to wear this.",
        ["I427"] = "Special Armor   Head  0.8 kg\nOrladin himself made this hood with\nthe power of magic built into it.\nIt takes less time to recover magic\npower after using a spell.",
        ["I428"] = "Special Armor   Head  1.5 kg\nThe helmet used by the legendary\nGarans. It will block the use of\nmagic power, but will increase the\nuser's physical strength.",
        ["I429"] = "Ordinary Armor   Head  5.5 kg\nIn the ancient past, the soldiers\nknown as the Dragon Knights\nwore this helmet. It has a high\ndefense.",
        ["I430"] = "Ordinary Armor   Head  4.1 kg\nThis helm is made with the rare\nmetal, Promeus, handed down by the\nDwarfs for centuries. The entire\narmor is made of Promeus.",
        ["I431"] = "Special Armor    Head  0.6 kg\nIchrius' Helm is made from the\nbrilliant rock which Ichrius found\nnear the tree of the Dragon King\nPlant. It heightens Light power.",
        ["I432"] = "Ordinary Armor   Body  5.3 kg\nThis body armor is standard issue\nfor the soldiers of the Verdite\nArmy. It is light, but not very\neffective against attack.",
        ["I433"] = "Ordinary Armor   Body  9.9 kg\nArmored Infantry of the Verdite\nArmy employed this strong\nprotective gear made of Iron.",
        ["I434"] = "Ordinary Armor   Body  4.2 kg\nThis is made of special alloy and\nis extremely lightweight. It is\nworn by officers of the Verdite\nArmy.",
        ["I435"] = "Special Armor    Body  4.O kg\nOrladin, the Great Archmage, gave\nthis armor to his disciple, Thedek,\nthe Fire Mage. The armor will\nprotect against fire magic.",
        ["I436"] = "Special Armor    Body  3.7 kg\nOrladin made this armor for\nhimself. It will decrease\nthe magical power necessary to\ncast a spell by one half.",
        ["I437"] = "Ordinary Armor   Body  11.5 kg\nThe armor is made with the rare\nmetal, Promeus, handed down by the\nDwarfs for centuries. If an entire\narmor is made of Promeus.",
        ["I438"] = "Special Armor     Body  6.O kg\nThe heavy armor of the legendary\nGarans. It is so thick that to cast\na spell through it will take twice\nthe normal amount of magic.",
        ["I439"] = "Special Armor     Body  3.8 kg\nIchrius' Armor is made from the\nbrilliant rock which Ichrius found\nnear the tree of the Dragon King\nPlant. It heightens earth power.",
        ["I441"] = "Ordinary Armor    Shield  1.2 kg\nThis shield is standard issue\nfor the soldiers of the Verdite\nArmy.",
        ["I442"] = "Ordinary Armor    Shield  1.8 kg\nThe Armored Infantry of the\nVerdite Army employed this\nstrong protective gear made\nof iron.",
        ["I443"] = "Special Armor     Shield  1.5 kg\nOrladin, the great Archmage, made\nthis shield. It will cause magic\npower to recover while walking\non the bare earth.",
        ["I444"] = "Ordinary Armor    Shield  5.O kg\nThis is the shield handed down\nin the High Elves' village for\ncenturies. It has the artwork of\nthe feather of Seath on it.",
        ["I445"] = "Ordinary Armor    Shield  2.2 kg\nThis is the wooden armor presented\nby the King of the East before the\ncontinent became divided. It has\ngreat defensive power.",
        ["I446"] = "Special Armor     Shield  2.3 kg\nOrladin made this guard for himself.\nThe shield is supposed to have\nseveral eyes, it must grow in power\nbefore it will display them though.",
        ["I447"] = "Special Armor     Shield  1.8 kg\nOrladin made this guard for himself.\nThe shield has several eyes and\nwill increase the power of light,\nbut will decrease physical strength.",
        ["I448"] = "Special Armor     Shield  3.2 kg\nThe shield of the legendary Garans.\nIt will hurl its user into utter\ndarkness but will increase defense\nagainst enemy magic.",
        ["I449"] = "Ordinary Armor    Shield  9.9 kg\nThis shield is made with the rare\nmetal, Promeus, handed down by the\nDwarfs for centuries. The entire\narmor is made of Promeus.",
        ["I450"] = "Special Armor     Shield  1.9 kg\nIchrius' Shield is made from the\nbrilliant rock which Ichrius found\nnear the tree of the Dragon King\nPlant. It heightens water power.",
        ["I453"] = "Ordinary Armor    Gloves  1.1 kg\nThese gloves are standard issue\nfor the soldiers of the Verdite\nArmy.",
        ["I454"] = "Ordinary Armor    Gloves  1.8 kg\nThe armored Infantry of the\nVerdite Army employed this\nstrong protective gear made\nof iron.",
        ["I455"] = "Ordinary Armor    Gloves  2.O kg\nThese gloves are made of the sacred\nmetal, Silver. When paralyzed by\nenemy magic, the gloves decrease\nthe time of paralysis.",
        ["I456"] = "Special Armor     Gloves  1.8 kg\nThese gloves were presented by the\nKing of the East. Wearing these\ngloves will decrease the weight\nof a weapon.",
        ["I457"] = "Special Armor     Gloves  2.2 kg\nUsing the Fire Mail as a model,\nThedek, the Fire Mage, made\nthese gloves. Wearing them will\nincrease the power of fire.",
        ["I458"] = "Special Armor     Gloves  1.6 kg\nThe legendary Garans used these\ngloves. The striking power of any\nweapon will increase, but so will\nthe weight of the weapon.",
        ["I459"] = "Ordinary Armor    Gloves  3.4 kg\nThese gloves are made with the rare\nmetal, Promeus, handed down by the\nDwarfs for centuries. The entire\narmor is made of Promeus.",
        ["I460"] = "Special Armor     Gloves  0.8 kg\nIchrius' Gloves are made from the\nrock which Ichrius found near the\ntree of the Dragon King. These\nlighten the weight of a weapon.",
        ["I462"] = "Ordinary Armor    Boots  1.9 kg\nThese boots are standard issue\nfor the soldiers for the Verdite\nArmy.",
        ["I463"] = "Ordinary Armor    Boots  2.2 kg\nThese boots protect both the feet\nand legs. They are used by the\nhigh ranking officers of the\narmy.",
        ["I464"] = "Ordinary Armor    Boots  2.9 kg\nThese boots are made of sacred\nsilver. They are worn by high\nranking officers. They have high\nresistance against poison.",
        ["I465"] = "Special Armor     Boots  2.O kg\nThese boots were made by Zul\nArifin. Wearing these boots will\nmake it possible to cross the Water\nBridges created by Orladin.",
        ["I466"] = "Ordinary Armor    Boots  1.6 kg\nThese boots will protect from\nspecialized attacks but will make\nmoving around more cumbersome and\nwill make running impossible.",
        ["I467"] = "Special Armor     Boots  1.6 kg\nThese boots were presented by the\nKing of the East. They will allow\nyou to run like the wind without\nfatigue.",
        ["I468"] = "Ordinary Armor    Boots  3.4 kg\nThese boots are made with the rare\nmetal, Promeus, handed down by the\nDwarfs for centuries. The entire\narmor is made of Promeus.",
        ["I469"] = "Special Armor     Boots  1.2 kg\nIchrius' Boots are made from the\nbrilliant rock. They increase Wind\npower & protect against poison\nand paralysis.",
        ["I471"] = "Special Armor     Others\nWhen the Dwarfs lived in the woods,\nthe spirits of the woods gave the\nDwarfs this bracelet. This bracelet\nwill increase physical strength.",
        ["I472"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThis ring has a spell cast upon\nit which will increase all magical\npowers in exchange for losing\nphysical strength.",
        ["I473"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThe Elves who lived in poisonous\nmarshes made the ring to protect\nthemselves against the poison.",
        ["I474"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThis bracelet is embedded with a\njewel from the brilliant stone that\nIchrius discovered. It helps the\nwearer to recover from a wound.",
        ["I475"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThis bracelet has Darkness inside\nit. It will protect against magic\nattacks, and will heighten the\npower of all magic except Light.",
        ["I476"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThe legendary Garans made this ring\nto protect against paralysis. This\nwill decrease the duration of\nparalysis.",
        ["I478"] = "Special Armor     Others\nShudom made this by harnessing the\nlife power of the earth.\nIt will heal a wounds and increase\ndefense against specialized attacks.",
        ["I479"] = "Special Armor     Others\nKing Harvine, the King of Wind,\nmade this magical necklace to\nincrease the power of wind magic.",
        ["I480"] = "Special Armor     Others\nShudom, the Archmage of Earth,\nmade this ring to increase Earth\nmagic by sealing the power of the\nearth inside of it.",
        ["I481"] = "Special Armor     Others\nThis Talisman was made by Leon\nShore. Made from the light crystal,\nit will protect against almost all\nspecialized attacks.",
        ["I482"] = "Special Armor     Others\nOrladin trapped the fairies sent by\nthe gods to spy on him, and sealed\nthem inside this crown. The spirit\nis used to find the secret entrance.",
        ["I485"] = "General Items\nThis is the map of the kingdom\nof Verdite. It is still fairly\naccurate as it was made when\nAlfred was crowned King.",
        ["I486"] = "Special Item\nThe power of the fairy of the\nwoods is sealed inside. The map\nwill automatically chart which\nroads have been traveled.",
        ["I489"] = "General Item\nThis is the message written by\nLyn, the Elf merchant, before she\nembarked on a trip to Garan.",
        ["I490"] = "General Item\nThis is the message written by Leon\nwhen he realized it would cost him\nhis life to build the combinations\nfor the key of Ichrius.",
        ["I491"] = "Special Item\nThis item shows its user the truth\nof anything viewed through it. Only\n7 exist in all of the world.",
        ["I492"] = "General Item\nThis is the key to the switches\nfound in the maze forest of Varde.",
        ["I494"] = "Recovery Item\nThis herb will heal the wounded\nbody.",
        ["I495"] = "Recovery Item\nThis is the medicinal herb which\nis used to eradicate poison. The\nbody will be healed of injuries\nwhen poison is removed.",
        ["I496"] = "Recovery Item\nThis liquid will completely heal\nthe injured body.",
        ["I497"] = "Recovery Related Special Item\nThis crystal gives total recovery\nto the injured body and mind. This\nfruit of the Dragon Tree is useful\nfor sudden damaging body changes.",
        ["I498"] = "Recovery Related Special Item\nThis red gem contains magical\npower and will cure conditions\ninflicted by magical attacks as\nwell as instantly cure paralysis.",
        ["I499"] = "Recovery Related Special Item\nThis is the stone which contains\nthe moon's magical power. It is\neffective for regaining magic\npoints.",
        ["I500"] = "Special Effect Item\nThe magical power of high level\nmages has been sealed inside this\ngem. Verdite will increase all\nareas of magical power.",
        ["I501"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the fruit of a tree which\ncontains earth's life power. This\nwill increase man's physical\nstrength.",
        ["I502"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis fruit was said to have been\nplanted by Vallad. Eating this\nfruit will cause Intelligence to\nincrease.",
        ["I503"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the magic stone\ncontaining fire magic. The magical\npower of fire will increase if you\nuse this stone.",
        ["I504"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the magic stone\ncontaining earth magic. The magical\npower of earth will increase if you\nuse this stone.",
        ["I505"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the magic stone\ncontaining water magic. The magical\npower of water will increase if you\nuse this stone.",
        ["I506"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the magic stone\ncontaining wind magic. The magical\npower of wind will increase if you\nuse this stone.",
        ["I507"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is the magic stone\ncontaining light magic. The magical\npower of light will increase if you\nuse this stone.",
        ["I508"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is a special flask of crystal.\nAn ordinary flask cannot contain\nwater from the Recovery Fountain\nas it will evaporate.",
        ["I509"] = "Healing Related Special Item\nThis is the flask containing sacred\nblue healing water, which is\neffective to partially heal the\nwounded body.",
        ["I510"] = "Healing Related Special Item\nThe flask contains sacred gold\nhealing water, which is\neffective to heal the wounded\nbody, mind and any dysfunction.",
        ["I513"] = "Special Effect Item\nMarilyn made this charm for her son\nas she prayed for his soul. It will\nbreak the spell of evil which has\nimprisoned her son's soul.",
        ["I514"] = "General Item\nThis is the very special precious\nmetal handed down by the Dwarfs.\nIt makes excellent weapons as\nwell as armor.",
        ["I515"] = "Special Effect Item\nThe Holy Sword of your father, it\nwas broken 10 years ago. Alexander\nput his entire being upon the sword\nto seal the castle.",
        ["I516"] = "Special Effect Item\nOrladin trapped the fairies sent by\nthe gods to spy on him and\npetrified them.",
        ["I517"] = "General Item\nThis is the special herb which\nis effective for sudden illness\nat the Passage of Poison. It will\npurify infected blood.",
        ["I518"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis needle contains Orladin's\npower. It can restore anything that\nhas become petrified.",
        ["I519"] = "Special Effect Item\nAlex found this in the Dragon Foun-\ntain, at the center of the castle\ncourtyard. He gave the ring to Lyn\nwho has been wanting to return it.",
        ["I520"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is one of the three seals of\nIchrius. It will lead to the\nFountain of Healing.",
        ["I521"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is one of the three seals of\nIchrius. It will lead to the\nFountain of Healing.",
        ["I522"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis is one of the three seals of\nIchrius. It will lead to the\nFountain of Healing.",
        ["I523"] = "Special Effect Item\nThis key has 3 essential parts: the\nEye, Wing, and Crown of Ichrius.\nThis combined key leads to multiple\nplaces.",
        ["I524"] = "The Key for the Door\nThis very important key will\nunlock the doors which lead to\nVerdite Castle. There are four\naltogether.",
        ["I525"] = "The Key for the Treasure Chest\nKing Alfred I had this key made\nfor the royal family. This key is\nneeded to open the royal family's\ntreasure chest.",
        ["I526"] = "Door and Chest Key\nThis key is needed to open the door\nat the Temple of Orladin &\nis also needed to open Orladin's\ntreasure chest.",
        ["I527"] = "The Key for the Treasure Chest\nThis is the master key for most\nof the treasure chests. Most of\nthe time the key opens the\ntreasure chests.",
        ["I528"] = "The Key for the Treasure Chest\nThe key is for the specially made\ntreasure chests used often by the\nmerchants. The chests sometimes\ncontain valuable items.",
        ["I529"] = "The Key for the Treasure Chest\nThe key will release the magic\nspell cast on the lock. It will\nunlock the chest which has\nbeen magically sealed.",
        ["I530"] = "The Key for the Door\nThe key is for the door of the\ncastle prison. Silviera is\nsupposed to have the same\nkey.",
        ["I531"] = "The Key for the Door\nThis key is for the pedestals built\nupon the defense walls. In order\nto prevent the invasion of the evil\ncreatures.",
        ["I532"] = "The Key for the Door\nThis is a very important key\nwhich will open the gates and\ndoors in the Dwarves' caves.",
        ["I533"] = "Special Effect Item\nOrladin could actually create\nliving beings. In his dungeon,\nhe had his own head cut off and\nmade into a mysterious key.",
        ["I534"] = "The Key for the Door\nThis is the key for the house of\nthe Elf merchant, Lyn. The Elf\nmerchants usually carry unusual\nitems.",
        ["I537"] = "General Item\nThese arrows must be used with\nthe large bow.",
        ["I538"] = "Special Effect Item\nThese arrows must be used with\nthe Elchris Bow. The arrows will\ncontinue to chase their target\nforever.",
        ["I539"] = "General Item\nThis is the common currency used\nin Verdite.",
