        ["I690"] = "Attribute: Fire  Level: 1\nThis 1st level fire spell allows\nyou to make a ball of fire in your\nhands & hurl it at the enemy.",
        ["I691"] = "Attribute: Fire  Level: 2\nThis 2nd level fire spell lets you\ncreate a wall. This wall, when cast\nat an enemy, will surround it with\na burning wall of fire.",
        ["I692"] = "Attribute: Fire  Level: 3\nThis 3rd level fire spell allows\nyou to make several fire balls with\nyour hands and throw them all at\nyour enemy.",
        ["I693"] = "space",
        ["I694"] = "Attribute: Fire  Level: 4\nFlame was devised by Orladin. This\nlevel 4 fire spell creates a fire\ntornado with Birds of Fire flying\naround destroying enemies.",
        ["I695"] = "Attribute: Fire  Level: 5\nThedek, Fire Mage, devised this\nmagic. This highest level fire\nspell summons Black Flame\nDragons to consume your foe.",
        ["I696"] = "Attribute: Earth  Level: 2\nThis earth spell will enable you to\ncall upon the rocks in the earth.\nThe rocks coming out of the earth\nwill be hurled against the enemy.",
        ["I697"] = "Attribute: Earth  Level: 3\nThis Earth magic is caused by\nutilizing the vibrations of the\nearth. This vibration, in turn,\nwill produce shock waves.",
        ["I698"] = "Attribute: Earth  Level: 4\nThis is an advanced magic\nconnecting the earth with the sky.\nThis powerful Earth magic will\ncause meteors to fall on the enemy.",
        ["I699"] = "Attribute: Earth  Level: 5\nDevised by Shudom, it is the most\nadvanced earth magic. This spell\nsummons two headed dragons which\nwill fly forth shooting earth waves.",
        ["I700"] = "space",
        ["I701"] = "Attribute: Water  Level: 3\nThis haze will become a mixture\nof poison and water vapor in the\natmosphere. Then the fine mist\nwill be blown against the enemy.",
        ["I702"] = "Attrjbute: Water  Levej: 4\nThjs js an advanced water magjc of\npurjfjcatjon. jt wjjj trap enemjes\njnsjde a cojumn of water & \"purjfy\"\nthem.",
        ["I703"] = "Attribute: Wind  Level: 1\nSharp wind knives will fly through\nthe air, cutting the enemy.",
        ["I704"] = "space",
        ["I705"] = "Attribute: Wind  Level: 3\nThis will cause a tornado by\ncreating a sudden warp in the\natmosphere. The tornado will be\ndirected against the enemy.",
        ["I706"] = "Attribute: Wind  Level: 4\nOrladin saw a vision of a dragon in\na dream. This magic reproduces that\nvision. A great ice dragon will\nappear and attacks your foe.",
        ["I707"] = "Attribute: Wind  Level: 5\nDevised by King Harvine, this is\nthe most advanced Wind magic. It\nsummons ghost beasts which shoot\nout shock waves.",
        ["I708"] = "space",
        ["I709"] = "Attribute: Light  Level: 3\nThis Light spell releases a\nlightning bolt of great light power.\nThe bolt will produce shock waves\nand ightning, destroying the enemy.",
        ["I710"] = "Attribute: Light  Level: 4\nThis level 4 Light spell utilizes\npower inherent in the atmosphere.\nThis energy is converted into bombs\nwhich fall on the enemy.",
        ["I711"] = "Attribute: Light  Level: 5\nThis is his most advanced light\nspell. It uses all seven colors of\nlight and will purify the utter\ndarkness.",
        ["I712"] = "space",
        ["I713"] = "Attribute: Earth  Level: 1\nThis first level earth healing\nspell will borrow the power of\nthe Great Earth to bring healing\nto the injured body.",
        ["I714"] = "space",
        ["I715"] = "Attribute: Water  Level: 1\nThis first level defensive water\nmagic will neutralize the poison\nin the body by utilizing the\nspirit of water.",
        ["I716"] = "Attribute: Water  Level: 2\nThis second level defensive water\nmagic will increase resistance\nagainst fire attacks.",
        ["I717"] = "Attribute: Water  Level: 5\nThe only level 5 defensive spell.\nTaking its power from the holy mind,\nit protects the righteous from evil.",
        ["I718"] = "Attribute: Wind   Level: 2\nThis second level defensive wind\nmagic will reduce the amount of\ndamage inflicted by an enemy.",
        ["I719"] = "Attribute: Light  Level: 1\nThis will bring all the light in\nthe universe into one, lighting\nthe path for the righteous.",
        ["I720"] = "Attribute: Light  Level: 2\nThis blessing is from the holy\npower of those who are pure in\nheart. It will heal the wounds of a\nwarrior.",
        ["I788"] = "Leon is certainly a master. Your\nsword contains a spirit within &\nhas great power. It has the power\nof light and is a rare sword\nwhich you will find very useful\nlater on. This one will be needed\nto make the key of Ichrius.",
        ["I789"] = "This sword, along with the Shiden\nsword, was given to King Harvine\nby the King of the East. Harvine\nwas fond of this sword and gave\nit the power of wind. It has an\nextremely sharp blade and is the\nlast sword to carry his name.",
        ["I790"] = "This is the sword of the Garan\npeople. According to legend, the\ntribe was destroyed because they\nincurred the wrath of a dragon.\nThe method for crafting the blade\nwas unfortunately destroyed with\nthe people. It has earth power.",
        ["I791"] = "Not actually a weapon, this rod\nwas presented to the King by Zul\nArifin. It is endowed with water\nmagic because it lay at the\nbottom of the lake for over 1000\nyears. It has no striking power,\nbut it has powerful magic.",
        ["I792"] = "Thedek presented this rod to\nOrladin who, for some unexplained\nreason, threw it in the lava\nriver. It was found by Garnabus\nwho gave it to Ed Edmund, his\ncaretaker. It carries water magic\n& will increase its user's power.",
        ["I793"] = "This is an amplification tool for\nphysical and mental strength.\nIt is the helmet of the Garans\nwhich will nullify the use of\nmagic, but will increase physical\nstrength. Those who love magic\nmay not like this tool.",
        ["I794"] = "In the ancient past the warriors\nknown as the Dragon Knights\nwore this kind of helmet. It is\nmade of the scales of a dragon.\nMolest of these helmets left\nValicia along with the Dragon\nKnights. This is very rare.",
        ["I795"] = "This helm is made from the rock\nwhich Ichrius found near the tree\nof the Dragon King Plant. It will\nheighten the power of light,\nincrease resistance against\nspecialized attacks, and protect\nagainst paralysis.",
        ["I796"] = "Orladin made this shield for\nhimself with the powers of magic\nbuilt into it. The shield is\nsupposed to contain several eyes.",
        ["I797"] = "This is the shield of the Garans.\nIt will hurl its user into utter\ndarkness, but will increase\ndefense against enemy magic. The\nGarans were destroyed partly\nbecause they were not skilled in\nfighting with magic.",
        ["I798"] = "There are two items in verdite\nwith the name \"Evil\" attached to\nthem. One is the Evil Crescent &\nthe other is the Evil Ring. This\nring has a tremendous power, but\nyou must be careful because the\nring may have a spell cast on it.",
        ["I799"] = "King Harvine made this magical\nnecklace to increase wind magic.\nMany talismen went to his palace\nto beg to be granted this neclace\nto increase their power of magic.",
        ["I800"] = "Shudom, the Archmage of Earth,\nmade this jewel into a ring to\nincrease the power of earth\nmagic. The jewel harnesses the\nearth's natural magical power\nand is known as his greatest\nmasterpiece.",
        ["I801"] = "This Talisman was made by Leon\nShore. Made from light crystal,\nthe wing will protect against\nalmost all specialized attacks.\nThe creation of this tool was\nalmost a prediction of what would\nhappen to Verdite later.",
        ["I802"] = "Orladin captured the fairies sent\nby Seath and Guyra and sealed\nthem inside this crown. The power\nof magic is needed to reveal the\nsecret entrance. It's a creation\nresulting from Orladin's love of\npractical jokes",
        ["I803"] = "Fairies were sent as Guyra's\nmessengers to spy on Orladin,\nbut the Great Archmage captured\nthem and encased them in stone.\nThey are the connecting point to\nGuyra but, encased in stone, they\nare quite useless.",
        ["I804"] = "This very important key will\nunlock the doors which lead to\nVerdite Castle. Endt is the only\nperson who knows how to get to\nthe first floor of the castle\nwithout using a key.",
        ["I805"] = "This key is to the door of the\ncastle prison. Silviera had this\nsame key at one point. Inside the\njail, there is a painting done by\nan artist who was imprisoned\nbecause he refused to draw a\nportrait of the King.",
        ["I806"] = "Orladin, the Great Archmage, had\nbecome powerful enough to create\nliving beings. In his dungeon,\nhe had his own head cut off and\nmade into a mysterious key. By\nusing this key, you can discover\nyour destiny and gain power.",
        ["I810"] = "Quist\nA few High Elves lived here, but\nthere were no humans. On the Day\nof the Seal, a few families moved\nhere as they followed Leon to get\nfarther from the castle.",
        ["I811"] = "Quist Cemetery\nThis cemetery contains the tomb\nof Noel, Queen of Verdite. Many\ngood people have lost their lives\nduring these harsh times, but\nher's has been felt the most\nthroughout the kingdom.",
        ["I812"] = "Small Shrine of the Elves\nBefore most of the Elves fled to\nother countries, they used to\nworship Seath in these small\nshrines.",
        ["I813"] = "The Statue of the Hero\nThis is the statue of Silviera.\nHe was a great commander & saved\nmany lives -- The citizens carved\nthis statue to honor their great\nhero. Those who were responsible\nfor erecting this monument have\nmostly disappeared or died.",
        ["I814"] = "Ancient Battleground\nOn this battlefield, the garrison\nled by Silviera fought fiercely\nagainst the evil creatures. Also\nin this very location, King\nAlfred once led the Verdite Army\nagainst the first wave of evil\ncreatures many years ago.",
        ["I815"] = "The Garrison Barracks\nThe garrison, led by Commander\nSilviera, used these barracks for\ntheir housing. Even those who had\nnever used weapons were recruited\nto this army, and most never\nreturned from battle.",
        ["I816"] = "The Forest of Varde\nThis used to be a part of Seath's\nForest and many Elves lived here.\nMolest of them moved to Mlelanat\nIsland and, after the radical\nchange in the King, the rest fled\nto other countries. Varde, Chief\nof the Woods, remains here alone.",
        ["I817"] = "Ralugo\nThis was the birthplace of King\nAlfred. The stone monument at the\ninn was erected here at the time\nof his coronation. A handful of\npeople who failed to flee now\nreside here.",
        ["I818"] = "The Palace of the Wind\nNo one may enter this palace\nwithout the power of wind, John\nCreel will make sure of that!\nOnce inside, demons conjured by\nThedek await trespassers and\nmagical candlesticks await the\nsacred Flame of Harvine.",
        ["I819"] = "The Cave of Shudom\nShudom, Archmage of the Earth,\nwas one of the two disciples of\nOrladin, the Great Archmage.\nShudom used this cave as his\nplace of experimentation. He\ndeserted the cave after several\nfai!ed experiments.",
        ["I820"] = "The Path of Poison\nAmong many underground pathways\nin Verdite, this is the oldest.\nIt is thus called because the\npoison from the earth permeates\nthe tunnel. The members of the\nhighly prosperous Light Family\nused to frequent this place.",
        ["I821"] = "Lake Noel\nThis lake was named after the\nbeloved and beautiful Queen Noel.\nNo one visits the lake anymore,\nnot since the Archmage of Water,\nZul Arifin, removed the bridges\nto halt the demon traffic across\nthe lake.",
        ["I822"] = "The Path of Thieves\nMages and merchants used this\nunderground passage as a place to\nhide their precious belongings\nduring times of war. Due to the\nnumerous traps set to protect the\ntreasures, thieves are now the\nonly people who venture here.",
        ["I823"] = "The Cave of the Dwarf\nWhen the Dwarfs were chased from\nthe Land of Garan, many settled\nhere. Promeus was rumored to be\nfound here; however, to this day,\nnone has been discovered. The\nDwarfs began to migrate to other\ncountries & only two remain here.",
        ["I824"] = "The Village of Cason\nThis village is protected by the\nold swordsman, Olivier Veyrac,\nand by the steep cliffs\nsurrounding the village. For a\nwhile, villagers here enjoyed\npeace even after King Alfred's\ntransformation.",
        ["I825"] = "The Field of Ice\nThis field used to be a large\ngreen meadow, but, since the\narrival of the evil creatures of\nice, it has been frozen over into\na meadow of ice. Many excavations\nhave been going on recently, and\nthe field has a new appearance.",
        ["I826"] = "The Valley of Garan\nThis land was rich in Promeus,\nthe sacred metal of the Dwarves.\nMany Dwarves used to dwell here,\nbut now only two remain. The\nothers either fled or were eaten\nby the Garan Lizards, which ate\nDwarfs as their staple food.",
        ["I827"] = "The Ruin of the High Elves\nThe High Elves erected shrines\nnot only in Verdite, but in\nvarious other places as well. The\nancient Ruin here in the valley\nis the oldest. It is said that\nthe site had been inhabited since\nthe beginning of time.",
        ["I828"] = "The Maze Temple of Orladin\nThis is where Orladin lived his\nlife. It's also where Shudom and\nThedek learned their magic. No\none can explain why Orladin, who\nacquired such great power in The\nPlace of the Beginning, remained\nhere for most of his life.",
        ["I829"] = "The Place of the Beginning\nThis, the basement of the Maze\nTemple, is the birthplace of the\nHigh Elves. Ichrius obtained his\npower here and even built part of\nthis place. Orladin received his\npower here from Ichrius along\nwith the secrets to power.",
        ["I830"] = "The Passage of Death\nShortly before his downfall, the\nKing had several items hidden in\nthis passage and had traps set up\nto protect them. Since that time,\nhe has sent many people to the\npath to retrieve them, but none\nhave made it out alive.",
        ["I831"] = "The Hill of Prayer\nUpon this hill, just outside the\nouter wall of the castle, King\nAlfred and the Queen offered a\nprayer for peace. Since then the\nhill has been called the Hill of\nPrayer. Alex' tomb is located on\nthis hill, it is a sacred place.",
        ["I832"] = "The First Level of the Royal\nCemetery\nThe cemetery has deteriorated due\nto a lack of maintenance and has\nbecome a nest for evil. The King\nmoved the Dragon Spring inside\nthe castle walls for protection,\n& this area is remembered as the\nnostalgic place of King Alfred.",
        ["I833"] = "Sleeping Quarters of Guyra\nThis is the fifth level of the\nRoyal Cemetery. The dragon which\nappears there is actually Mlillia,\nthe projected shadow of Guyra.\nCreated by Guyra, Mlillia protects\nthis place where Guyra hopes to\nreturn to the earth.....",
        ["I834"] = "Verdite Castle\nThe courtyard of the castle used\nto be a place of great beauty and\ntranquillity. Alexander, as well\nas many others, used to walk here\nin the garden amongst the trees\nand come to stand by the Dragon\nSpr!ng to think.",
        ["I835"] = "The Ground Floor of the Castle\nBefore the transformation of the\nKing, visitors, poets, and noble-\nmen would frequent this visiting\narea. Laughter and conversation\nused to fill the air and even the\nKing would often come here to\ntalk with the people of Verdite.",
        ["I836"] = "The Basement of the Castle\nOnce a huge storage for food and\nweapons, the basement is now the\nsite of the castle dungeon.\nMerchants used to bring goods to\nthis place, but now the basement\nis quiet except for the wails of\nthe few remaining souls.",
        ["I837"] = "The Second Floor of the Castle\nIt was soon after Alex returned\nfrom the island that King Alfred\nchanged. The King had locked\nhimself inside his chamber after\nbecoming ill. Sounds of struggle\ncould be heard from inside, & the\nking who emerged seemed alien.",
        ["I838"] = "Seath's Space\nDragons, which were demigods,\ndwell in their own space\ndimension. Seath, who is half of\nVallad, is in his own space\ndimension similar to Guyra's.",
        ["I839"] = "The Commander's Room\nCommander Silviera's room\nremained unoccupied most of the\ntime because Silviera spent most\nof his time time fighting in the\nbattlefields.",
        ["I840"] = "Officers' Quarters\nMany distinguished knights were\nunder Silviera's command. Some of\nhis officers were even famous.\nWith his red sword, \"Flame,\"\nvice Commander Caine was one of\nthe most popular knights. But, he\nnever returned from battie.",
        ["I841"] = "Training Chamber\nSilviera was a skilled craftsman\nwhen it came to making traps. He\nbuilt this chamber of traps to\ntrain newly recruited soldiers,\nand offered prizes for soldiers\nwho could defeat them. No one\nwas eyer able to win a prize.",
        ["I842"] = "Underground Jail\nAt the end of the long battle,\nsome soldiers were overcome with\nfear and began to flee. Silviera\nhad to make this jail to imprison\nthose who tried to run away. it\npained him to do this, but duty\ndemanded reprimand for cowardice.",
        ["I843"] = "The Palace of King Harvine\nKing Harvine is the only King who\never successfully united the\nthree kingdoms of the North. He\nbuilt this palace as his home\naway from home and also as a\nmilitary post for the peripheral\nareas.",
        ["I844"] = "The Temple of Orladin\nThis temple within the maze is\nwhere Orladin spent his whole\nlife after receiving his power in\nthe Place of the Beginning. He\ntried to build something here,\nbut eventually went back to the\nPlace of the Beginning to die.",
        ["I845"] = "The House of Gigi\nGigi and her son moved here from\nMlelanat Island. On the day of the\nseal, they fled to Granatyki\nduring the commotion. They\nsuccessfully got away from the\nmonsters, as well as from Mlel\nMolerris, who was stalking Gigi.",
        ["I846"] = "The Cave of the Slime\nThis place was a cemetery for the\nDwarfs. After the demise of all\nbut two of the Dwarfs in Garan,\nthe Slimes began to multiply in\nthe damp, empty caverns. No one\nwould come around to this\ncemetery anymore.",
        ["I847"] = "Thedek's Room\nThedek used this room before he\nleft to work for King Harvine.\nIn Harvine's basement, he tried\nto conjure a new breed of Fire-\nDrake. The Dragons became angered\nand tore him to shreds before\nburning and eating his remains.",
        ["I848"] = "Shudom's Room\nShudom used this room while he\nwas learning from Orladin. He\nbuilt his own dungeon to continue\nhis experimentation with magic,\nbut he left abruptiy and moved to\nMlelanat Island when one of his\nexperiments went awry.",
        ["I849"] = "Orladin's Room\nOrladin had this room made for\nhimself, though he seldom used\nit. Shudom and Thedek finally\ngave up on their teacher and left\nthe Place of the Beginning\nbecause Orladin never came back\nup from the basement.",
        ["I850"] = "The Royal Cemetery\nEons ago, Dragon Warriors saved\nthe kingdom from the ancient evil\nof Verdite. This temple was built\nto enshrine them. In time, Kings\nalso used this temple as their\ncemetery. This is where Alfred\nfound the Moleonlight Sword.",
        ["I851"] = "Seath's Space\nDragons, which were demigods,\ndwell in their own space\ndimension. Seath, who is half of\nVallad, is in his own space\ndimension similar to Guyra's.",
    };

